in a massive interview with the Verge  valve shared the future of the steam  deck including what we should expect  from the steam deck too here are some  highlights from the conversation the  steam deck has been a wildly successful  product for valve which is incredible to  think of when you realize that Steam  Machines a spiritual predecessor to the  device that the company partnered with  PC manufacturers on and were designed as  computers for your living room crashed  and burned but it now seems that the  success of the steam deck has  revitalized valve's interest in the  steam machine as the team gears up to  make the handheld steam OS available to  third parties steam deck designer  Lawrence Yang explains that not only is  he excited by the handhelds that other  companies could make utilizing the  operating system but the team is looking  forward to manufacturers bringing back  steam machines with it while the steam  deck isn't the only handheld gaming  device on the market it's one of the  cheapest as well as the most powerful  however that's a about to change once  products like the Aya neo2 hit the scene  which utilize an AMD 6800u chip that in  testing has shown to provide more  performance than valve's own custom  aerith SOC steam deck designer Pierre Lu  Griffey isn't too worried about those  devices however as they've proven to be  way less power efficient than the steam  deck tests have shown that the AMD chip  would drain the steam deck's battery  around twice as quickly as its current  processing units does the team seems  happy with the steam deck's performance  which leads them to talk about what  performance on a steam deck 2 would look  like and according to Yang graffey the  performance would look a whole lot like  what you're getting on your current  steam deck it seems valve will be taking  a switch OLED route for its next device  iterations rather than something akin to  the mythical switch Pro by targeting  improvements to both the steam deck  screen and battery life and keeping  performance even with steam deck 1.0  stating that they'd only look to  increase perform  if there were quote significant gains to  be had that's a ton of interesting  details from the steam deck team but it  just scratches the surface of what was  shared so make sure to go check out the  full interview after watching this video  in that information wet your whistle and  speaking of information that wets our  whistles Spider-Man 2 has a more locked  down release window originally announced  as launching in 2023 on PS5 PlayStation  has confirmed that it is targeting a  full release next year for the game  following an accidental posting of a  wishlist page for the game as well as an  insomniac employee putting a full 2023  window on their personal website  PlayStation has confirmed that the end  of next year will indeed be the time  period the game will release barring any  delays please spider gods don't let  there be a delay so far we don't have  many details on what to expect from the  game but both its trailer and the new  announcement post heavily imply it will  feature both Peter Parker and Miles  Morales as playable characters the  trailer features the villain Venom as  well as voiceover from what seems to be  the villain Craven the hunter if both  those bad guys hint to you that this  will be a darker game than the first  you'd be right as Marvel game's Vice  President Bill Roseman equates the  sequel to The Empire Strikes Back  juxtaposed to what he describes as  Spider-Man 2018's A New Hope which  really is saying something if you've  played through the end of Spider-Man  2018 you know what else is dark space  the setting for bethesda's next game  Star field which we got a few tidbits of  info on around the game's factions  unlike previous Bethesda games where  aligning with certain factions would  generally lock you out of teaming up  with others it seems Starfield will  allow you to see and do every Mission  related to every faction in the game  regardless of whether the goals of a  faction oppose another's the faction  quests will also be more personal to the  player but the decisions they make will  still have far-reaching consequences and  their companions will have a quote a lot  of opinions and points of view about  what decisions you'll be making what do  you think about the idea of there being  a steam deck OLED versus a steam deck  Pro let us know in the comments below  we'll see you here for more Gamespot  news  [Music]
 

